nvda-rdp-linux (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New server side: NVDA on Windows, with RDAccess and mstsc, speaks and
    shows the braille of Orca in a GNOME 49+ session served by GNOME
    Remote Desktop, the remote login screen included.
  * Split into nvda-rdp-common, nvda-rdp-freerdp-plugin, nvda-rdp-client
    and nvda-rdp-server.
  * Man pages nvda-rdp-client(1) and nvda-rdp-server(7), with French
    translations.

